WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.301
After months of fierce and

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.068
bloody fighting,

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.837
Russian forces may be on the verge

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:04.504
of capturing

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.439
the eastern city of Borehamwood.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.974
Even as Russian fighter

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:08.842
surround the city,

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.011
Ukrainian commanders are not withdrawing

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.013
and instead calling on President Zelensky

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.614
to send in reinforcements.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.382
CNN's Alex

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.517
Marquardt is in eastern Ukraine.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.919
Mercenary fighters from the Wagner Group

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:20.787
were seen

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.188
planting their flag

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.357
in the eastern part of the city.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.126
Tell us about that

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.261
Well, hi there, Victor and Bianna.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.195
Well, in the past few

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.397
days, Russian forces

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.832
have made some progress at encircling

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.067
not major,

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.235
but they have been pressing

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.237
forward to the north and to the south

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:38.738
around the city

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.373
and then pressing into the city

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.341
from the east.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.043
We did see that new video

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.044
from the Viognier group.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:44.411
Remember,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.513
Wagner has been really leading the charge

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:47.213
when it comes

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.783
to Russian forces around Bermuda.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.018
They removed the Ukrainian flag

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:52.786
from a monument.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.754
They planted their own flag,

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.622
not the Russian flag,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.123
but the Wagner flag,

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.892
and raised their guns in the air.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.126
Meanwhile, we did hear from President

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.661
Zelensky's office tonight

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.796
saying that they continue

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.131
to defend their positions,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:05.765
defend the city

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.901
and they talk about reinforcing

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:08.802
their positions.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.804
They didn't talk about surrender,

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:11.571
but we have spent

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.273
a lot of time in that area over the past

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:13.606
few days.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:14.674
We spent a lot of time

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:15.241
on the main

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.309
supply route

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.178
between the neighboring town of Chelsea

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.879
VR and Back Mount.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.281
There's a lot of military traffic

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.382
on that road.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:22.849
I can tell you

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:25.285
that it is getting very difficult

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.121
to move in and out of dark mood.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.990
It is getting attacked by Russian forces.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.592
They blew up a bridge on that main

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.461
supply route just a couple of days ago.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.196
We were told by local officials today

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.064
that military engineers

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:40.233
have erected a temporary bridge

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.602
so troops are able to move forward

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.103
and back.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.405
People are able to come out and go in

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.340
But it is getting much more difficult.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.007
And Victor and Brianna,

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.243
you're starting to hear this line

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.978
despite the fact that no withdrawal

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.946
has been announced,

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.448
that even if Ukraine were to withdraw

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:56.850
that this would not actually be

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.351
a strategic victory

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:58.918
for Russia,

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.054
that they will have lost so many men,

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.489
they would have taken over this city

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.223
that doesn't actually

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.891
have any strategic value

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:08.394
that Ukraine is actually was able

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.263
to degrade Russian forces

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.731
and buy time for a planned.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:13.433
That at

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.434
the end of the day,

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.503
according to us, and Ukrainian officials,

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.338
it would not be that strategic

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.172
a victory

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:19.806
for Russia,

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.974
but it really would

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.176
be a loss for Ukraine.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.511
They also have lost

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.412
a lot of men in this fight.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.381
They've lost professional soldiers. Why?

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.749
While on the Russian side,

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.050
so many of

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.352
the people who have been killed

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.754
have been convicts in the mercenary group

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.724
So at the end of the day,

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.225
this would be a symbolic victory

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.360
for Russia.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.761
But it really is up for debate

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.863
how strategic it would be.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.531
One last thing

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:44.864
I did

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:45.932
speak with the deputy

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.300
mayor of Baruch today

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.868
who said there are still some

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.870
four to 5000 people

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.772
who are still in the city.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.107
They're trying to get as many out

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.509
as possible, around five to ten per day,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.278
if they're lucky.

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.179
The people in there,

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.181
he says they simply don't want to leave

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.182
because they say

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.583
they don't know where they would go.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.918
That they don't have any money.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:05.618
They're scared.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.119
They're scared,

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.987
scared to go out on that road.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.989
And he said that his overwhelming feeling

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.958
when thinking about his city right now

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.660
is fear and sadness.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.661
Victory on

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.228
this is a city

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.197
that was once home to tens of thousands

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.899
of Ukrainians. Alex Marquardt, thank you.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.001
Well, let's bring in

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.936
CNN's Oren Liebermann,

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.037
who is at the Pentagon.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.471
The or in the defense

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.639
secretary spoke out

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.441
about the situation in Baku today.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.109
What is he saying?

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.044
This really echoes

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:31.377
the point

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.812
that Alex was making there

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.947
about the strategic value

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:35.215
or lack thereof when it comes

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.482
to the city of Mahmoud.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.750
Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.118
who is now traveling in the Middle

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.320
East, said this wouldn't

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.188
be some strategic strategic victory

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:42.622
for Russia.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.590
Simply because there isn't

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.925
that much strategic value to Obama

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.227
just given its location.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:47.727
It doesn't

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.229
control the surrounding area

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:49.996
or have a lookout

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.965
that gives you a strategic advantage

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.266
and still Russia

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.267
is determined

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.368
to keep throwing as many lives

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.035
as it needs to.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.203
It is to take Mahmoud.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:57.837
But again,

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.839
Austin saying this wouldn't be a victory.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:00.873
Listen to what he had to say here.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.276
I would not view

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.577
that as a

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.413
as an operational or strategic setback.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:10.216
I think it's more of a symbolic

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.387
value than it is strategic

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.688
and operational value.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.091
What I do see on a daily basis is

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.126
the Russians continuing to pour

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:23.029
in a lot of ill trained

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.530
and ill equipped troops.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.666
And those troops are very quickly

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.768
meaning their demise.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:30.069
It is worth pointing out

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.371
that even if the city itself

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.972
doesn't have strategic value,

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.374
it is an important decision

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.542
where you decide where Ukraine that is

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.645
decides to fight Russian forces.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:38.978
Right now,

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.413
Ukraine is making that decision

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.948
to fight in the city of Mahmoud

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.383
and that is an important

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.417
strategic decision.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.485
Ukraine realizing

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.219
if they don't fight them

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:47.120
on the line in Bermuda

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.022
and they decide at some point to withdraw

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.857
and to move back towards the west.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.558
That will simply be the new line

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.793
at which they fight the Russians.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.427
And that perhaps

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.395
another reason

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:56.496
that they decided to hold

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.197
or at least fight for the city of Bermuda

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.065
as long as possible

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.099
as both sides suffer

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.101
very high losses here, Bianna and Victor.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.003
We're anticipating

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.838
an offensive from the Ukrainians

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.440
sometime this spring as well.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.608
Oren Liebermann, thank you.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.044
General Wesley

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:12.412
Clark is a CNN military

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:13.546
analyst and former

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.381
NATO supreme allied commander. General.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:16.516
Good to see you.

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:17.917
So I'm interested to get your take

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:18.551
because we heard

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.952
from the defense secretary today

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.688
saying that in his view,

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.855
a retreat from back

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.524
would not be an operational

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.793
or strategic setback for the Ukrainians.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.494
And yet, at the same day,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.128
we're hearing

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:31.197
that Ukrainian military officials

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.032
are advising President Zelensky

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:33.766
to continue

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.802
to send in reinforcements

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:38.271
to to fight for this city.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.306
Is that a mistake on their part

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.574
at this point?

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.077
Well, it's really hard to second

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:45.878
guess us beyond because we're not there.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.080
We don't see the terrain.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.915
We don't see the ground now.

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:50.516
If you look at port mode

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.219
and you look west, it's several miles

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:53.786
to the next

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.756
really good, defensible terrain location.

00:05:57.323 --> 00:06:00.760
And if they get there, if they fall back,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.363
they're going to have to hold their

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.931
falling back.

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:06.232
A withdrawal under pressure

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.300
is one of the most difficult

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.068
military operations.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:12.105
You suffer the risk of a catastrophic

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.974
collapse and big losses when you do this.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.443
So it does make some sense.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:18.244
And I can understand

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:19.612
the logic of the Ukrainians

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:21.781
in wanting to hold where they are

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.182
as long as they can

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.450
they are inflicting heavy,

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.652
heavy casualties on the Russians.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:27.920
We don't see

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.955
the answer is

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:31.224
we don't see what's behind

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:33.393
the initial Russian assault

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.827
We don't see the forces in depth

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.062
arrayed back there.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.997
We also don't know how

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.632
the Ukrainian command

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.534
is building up its own forces

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.102
for the counteroffensive

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:45.271
and how much it can whittle away.

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.507
That force is necessary

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:49.742
to reinforce and be moot.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.544
So there's a lot of intangibles here

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:51.911
and things

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:52.478
that we just don't

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:53.946
have the information on.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.149
I do agree with Secretary State.

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:58.418
It's probably not a great,

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.720
from our perspective, operational

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.088
or tactical loss

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.190
but it is a psychological blow

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.492
and a psychological lift for Moscow.

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:07.894
And at some point,

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:10.062
these Russian troops have to be defeated.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.764
They have to be held.

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.599
They have to be pushed back.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:14.834
And so from the Ukrainian

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:16.102
military perspective,

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.271
it's a very understandable position

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:21.207
to hold the line as long as possibly can

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:23.709
I'm glad you brought up that planned

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.411
spring offensive that everyone's

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:26.879
anticipating from the Ukrainians,

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:27.780
because I'm wondering,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.347
listen, from

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.649
a cost benefit perspective,

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:32.051
one could argue that the past few months

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:33.719
really did benefit Ukraine

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:35.755
to continue fighting in back mode

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.657
because you lost a lot of Russian men

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:38.958
and a lot of Russian troops

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.493
and ammunition as well.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:42.361
That they invested in their battle

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.062
for that city.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:44.730
But at some point,

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:45.865
it does turn

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.266
and you see the reflection

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:48.367
upon Ukrainians

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.970
who are also losing their troops

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.638
there at an enormous rate

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:53.873
and their ammunition.

00:07:53.873 --> 00:07:55.741
Do you think the longer they

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.743
maintain this fight for Obama,

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.145
do you think it could impact

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.346
whatever counteroffensive

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:00.947
they're planning

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:03.216
Well, it

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:05.051
certainly could, but

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:07.353
they have to hold in the east.

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:09.722
They do not want to surrender Donbas

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:11.190
if they do.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:11.824
They're just going to have

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:13.459
to fight further West.

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:14.360
So they've got prepared

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.461
defensive positions here.

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:16.429
They've got stockpiles.

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:18.097
They know the routes.

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.566
This is an advantageous way to hold

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.468
for as long as they can.

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:23.736
Look, we are

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:25.404
there's no doubt that the Russians

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:27.507
have superiority of artillery.

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:28.107
Well,

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:30.443
certainly Ostrom has acknowledged that.

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:31.978
The thing is, they're firing.

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:33.246
They have more artillery tubes

00:08:33.246 --> 00:08:35.281
and they're far more ammunition

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:37.483
on a daily basis than the Ukrainians.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.819
We just got to get them more help.

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.754
And until that time,

00:08:41.754 --> 00:08:42.221
they're going to have

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:43.589
a hard time holding.

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:45.725
And the Ukrainians are taking casualties.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.262
But this is war and it's their country,

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:50.730
and they want to hold it.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.164
It is proving to be very difficult

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:54.901
to procure the amount of ammunition

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:55.801
that that Ukraine

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.303
is requiring at this point.

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:59.505
Here's how one military expert

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:02.008
described Russia as at all costs.

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:03.543
Battle for Obama.

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:05.411
Assuming that Ukrainians

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:06.679
at some point do retreat.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:07.513
Here's what he wrote.

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.181
The reality is that if the Russians do

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:09.982
capture Obama,

00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:11.317
they are seizing rubble

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:12.451
It is a town with minimal

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:13.519
strategic importance,

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:15.388
with almost no remaining infrastructure

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:17.290
to support an occupying force

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.691
that the Russians have invested

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:19.425
so much in.

00:09:19.425 --> 00:09:20.059
Its capture

00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:21.260
speaks volumes

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.663
about their poor strategy in this war.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.398
Would you agree with that assessment?

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:27.366
I'm a little

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:28.801
cautious about that assessment.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:29.201
The honor,

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:30.670
because it is written

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.838
from the Western perspective.

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:34.874
If you had 500,000 people

00:09:34.874 --> 00:09:36.108
and you lost 30,000

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:37.176
people, 40,000

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:37.944
people in a month,

00:09:37.944 --> 00:09:39.879
and you talk about what you might say

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:40.980
that's insignificant,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.848
If you were a Russian commander,

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.550
now, if you're an American commander

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:45.718
or Ukrainian commander

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:47.153
and you're losing 30,000 troops

00:09:47.153 --> 00:09:48.487
over that piece of ground,

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:49.689
that's really significant.

00:09:49.689 --> 00:09:51.424
But if you're a Russian commander

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:53.392
and they're pushing those troops forward

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.595
and they use them up usual, use them off

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.164
and you get a break through in dark mode,

00:09:58.164 --> 00:10:00.066
or you significantly degrade

00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:01.634
the Ukrainians

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:03.936
on balance, from the Russian perspective,

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.605
it might be worth it.

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:06.572
So I think we have to be

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:09.475
a little cautious about critiquing

00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:12.178
Russian tactics from our perspective.

00:10:13.079 --> 00:10:14.580
Yeah, from Russia's perspective,

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.182
these troops are expendable.

00:10:16.182 --> 00:10:18.684
There's talk about another conscription

00:10:18.684 --> 00:10:20.753
perhaps coming this summer.

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.622
General Wesley Clark, thank you so much.

00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:23.522
Always great to have you

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:24.790
on and your analysis.

